AFV Fibers copies no third-party code and runs no model. The fibre files it reads were made with:

- Qual's AFV V2 fibre model, https://huggingface.co/Qualzz20/afv_fiber_9um_v2 (checkpoint sha256
  b8519a4ce4044c93ed98af0c278628fdcdfdd8808275b3c8becd7211f38b7967): Apache License 2.0, by Qual (Qualzz).
- Qual's AVF_SPLINE_GENERATOR, https://github.com/Qualzz/AVF_SPLINE_GENERATOR at commit
  3c8b73628ca56cb28042b9b2e79439b2e1c693d2: Apache License 2.0, by Qual (Qualzz). Its .afv format is the VC3D fiber
  collection, version 1.

Scan data: AFV Fibers reads CT scans from the Vesuvius Challenge open data, licensed CC BY-NC 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/). Giorgio Angelotti, Stephen Parsons, Sean Johnson, Elian Rafael
Dal Prà, Johannes Rudolph, Paul Tafforeau, Alessandro Mirone, Paul Henderson, Hendrik Schilling, Forrest McDonald,
David Josey, Youssef Nader, C. Seth Parker, W. Brent Seales. Vesuvius Challenge: CT Scans of Herculaneum Papyri.
Vesuvius Challenge. https://scrollprize.org/data

The six fibre datasets (SharpMeow/<scan>-afv-fibers) and every picture the page shows of them are model output
computed from that data, so they are derived data under CC BY-NC 4.0 as well. Sets in the Catalog tab belong to their
makers and are linked, not copied.
